<task id="068" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>D-63: remaining sprk_finalduedate readers judge and show sprk_duedate (playbook, VisualHost card, CalendarVisual), own PR</title>
    <phase>8 Remaining cleanup and repairs</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes a live playbook node's query (Dataverse data) and client code; behaviour users see.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Own worktree off origin/master; files listed in notes/065-finalduedate-readers.md only.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>098</deps>
    <tags>frontend,dataverse,ai,separate-pr</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply owner decision D-63 (2026-10-07): sprk_finalduedate is informational only EVERYWHERE. Change the three remaining places that judge or display by it so they use sprk_duedate.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE engineer. A rescheduled task must not be called overdue by its old date.</role>
  <goal>(1) The live notification playbook node "Query Overdue Tasks" (id 348b6395-a171-f111-ab0d-7ced8ddc4a05) flags a task overdue only when sprk_duedate is before the recipient's today; (2) the VisualHost due-date card shows and judges sprk_duedate only; (3) CalendarVisual uses sprk_duedate when no date field is configured.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-27 made sprk_duedate the one due date for the Do lane, Reschedule and the Daily Briefing (PR #1359, task 065 folded into 098). Task 098 found three more readers still preferring or falling back to sprk_finalduedate; the inventory with file:line is notes/065-finalduedate-readers.md. Owner decision D-63 (2026-10-07): apply D-27 to all three; the playbook data change is approved by that decision.</background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner">D-63: the playbook node change is approved Dataverse data change in spaarkedev1 only. Record the node's before/after query text. Change only that node's date condition; do not touch other playbook nodes or other playbooks. Record the per-environment step (the playbook row ships with its owning solution) — do not export/import solutions yourself.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Base on origin/master AFTER PR #1359 merges (this task depends on 098). If #1359 has not merged when you start, STOP and report. Keep the "today" boundary per D-25 (recipient's time zone via the helper 098 added); do not reintroduce UTC.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Own PR to master. The blocking Tier 1 Xrm capability guard applies to any getXrm use. PCF builds via scripts/Invoke-PcfBuildProd.ps1 (npm run build:prod; pcf-scripts exits 0 on failure — judge by output). Bump VisualHost PCF version per the PCF deployment guide if the control changes. Never use --no-verify or bare git stash. You cannot write .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level per root CLAUDE.md section 8.</step>
    <step order="1">Read notes/065-finalduedate-readers.md; confirm the three readers on current master.</step>
    <step order="2">Change the VisualHost due-date card and CalendarVisual default; tests that fail on the old fallback (America/New_York jest environment from 098).</step>
    <step order="3">Change the playbook node's query in spaarkedev1; read it back; prove live with a zz-068- task whose final due date has passed but whose due date has not (no overdue notification candidate) and the reverse; delete test rows.</step>
    <step order="4">Build, tests, Xrm guard, Step 9.5 gates; open the PR against master; CI green; do not merge.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The "Query Overdue Tasks" node's condition references sprk_duedate only; before/after recorded; a rescheduled task (due in future, final due past) is not selected; an overdue task (due past) is selected — proven live, test rows deleted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The VisualHost due-date card and CalendarVisual never read sprk_finalduedate to decide what to show; tests fail on the old fallback.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No other playbook node or reader changed; git grep for sprk_finalduedate shows only informational uses, listed in the PR body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A PR against master is open with CI green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The playbook node's query cannot be changed without altering another node or the playbook's structure.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>Created 2026-10-07 by the main session on owner decision D-63 (from task 098's report).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
